            <div xml:id="d467">

                <pb facs="0609" n="497" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg497"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/7571: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-12-25T11:00:00+08:00">December 25, 1935—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 25—9 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>793. My December 24, 5 p.m. and December 24, 7 p.m. Following departure of two
                    trainloads of students Chinese authorities succeeded in dispersing student
                    groups at North Station and so far as is known effected dispersal without
                    serious injury to anyone.</p>
                <p>1. Train stopped at Kunshan about 50 miles from here due to alleged engine
                    trouble and the other at Soochow on a similar pretext. Chinese authorities
                    thereupon commenced to negotiate with the students and endeavored to extract
                    from them a guarantee of good behavior and a promise to refrain from further
                    demonstrations if they were taken back to Shanghai. Reliably informed this
                    morning that the students have refused thus far to give the desired guarantee
                    and that negotiations <pb facs="0610" n="498" xml:id="pg498"/> are continuing;
                    also reliably reported that two small groups of students are engaged this
                    morning in lecturing and distributing handbills in the Nantao and Siccawei areas
                    and that they may attempt to enter the Settlement later. Situation generally
                    easier.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Department and Nanking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
